# Without this file the build context is the whole working tree — roughly 900 MB
# on a developer machine, sent to the daemon on every build.
#
# It is also a correctness problem, not only a speed one. The Dockerfile does
# `COPY backend/ ./backend/` *after* installing dependencies, so a host
# node_modules would overwrite the container's own install with binaries built
# for the wrong platform. And DATA_DIR defaults to ./data in development, which
# means a developer's live tally.db sits inside the copied directory.
#
# The published image never included either — only `dist` is copied out of the
# build stage — but nothing about that was deliberate, and one refactor would
# have changed it.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Always rebuilt inside the image; copying a stale one in is how a
# build silently ships yesterday's code.
dist
**/dist

# Local databases and uploads. DATA_DIR defaults to ./data outside the container.
data
**/data

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Tests, docs and tooling: none of it runs in the image.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/vitest.config.ts
docs
*.md
!README.md

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
